Hybrid Inheritance

    Definition :
        Hybrid inheritance is a combination of two or more inheritance types.

    Example
        Single AND Hierarchical = Hybrid

    Diagram
                     Animal
                    /      \
                 Dog       Cat
                   |
                 Puppy

    This contains
        Hierarchical and Single Hence, Hybrid.



    Another Example

                     Employee
                    /       \
              Developer    Tester
                    |
             SeniorDeveloper

    Contains
        Hierarchical, Multilevel Hence,Hybrid.


Q1. What is Hierarchical Inheritance?

    One parent class is inherited by multiple child classes.

Q2. Does Java support Multiple Inheritance?

    No, not through classes. It supports it through interfaces.

Q3. What is the Diamond Problem?

    It is the ambiguity that occurs when a child inherits the same method from two parent classes.

Q4. What is Hybrid Inheritance?

    A combination of two or more inheritance types (for example, hierarchical + multilevel).

Q5. Does Java support Hybrid Inheritance?

    Not using classes. Hybrid inheritance is achieved in Java through interfaces.